 ### Slow Growing Subdivision Wavelet Transform
-A wavelet transform for volumetric subdivision meshes based on slow growing subdivision connectivity rules, using a lifting scheme [S1]. It differs from Generalized Linear B-Spline Wavelets by smoothing original vertices using neighbor positions rather than wavelet coefficients. The decomposition step computes tier $k+1$ vertices $v^{(k+1)}$ from tier $k$ vertices $v^{(k)}$ using the formula $v^{(k+1)} = \alpha v^{(k)} + \frac{1-\alpha}{m} \sum v$, where the sum is over vertices $v$ in $E(v^{(k+1)})$ (edge-connected vertices in the tier $k+1$ mesh) and $m$ is the count of such vertices [S1]. The parameter $\alpha$ controls the shape and stability of the wavelet basis functions [S1]. The set $E(v^{(k+1)})$ includes both tier $k$ and new tier $k+1$ vertices, affecting $m$ [S1].
